@host = http://localhost:5025

### 1. Create asset
POST {{host}}/api/assets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetTag": "LAP-0012",
  "name": "Dell Latitude 5440",
  "category": "Laptop",
  "serialNumber": "DL5440-XYZ123",
  "purchaseDate": "2026-01-15"
}

### Update asset (status is optional: Available / UnderRepair / Retired)
PUT {{host}}/api/assets/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetTag": "LAP-0012",
  "name": "Dell Latitude 5440 (16GB)",
  "category": "Laptop",
  "serialNumber": "DL5440-XYZ123",
  "purchaseDate": "2026-01-15",
  "status": "Available"
}

### List assets
GET {{host}}/api/assets

### 2. Create employee
POST {{host}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeCode": "EMP-001",
  "fullName": "Ravi Kumar",
  "email": "ravi.kumar@company.com",
  "department": "Engineering"
}

### Update employee
PUT {{host}}/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeCode": "EMP-001",
  "fullName": "Ravi Kumar",
  "email": "ravi.kumar@company.com",
  "department": "Platform Engineering",
  "isActive": true
}

### 3. Allocate asset 1 to employee 1
POST {{host}}/api/allocations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetId": 1,
  "employeeId": 1,
  "remarks": "Issued for onboarding"
}

### Open allocations
GET {{host}}/api/allocations?active=true

### Assets currently held by employee 1
GET {{host}}/api/employees/1/assets

### 4. Return (returnCondition: Good or Damaged)
POST {{host}}/api/returns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "allocationId": 1,
  "returnCondition": "Good",
  "remarks": "Returned with charger"
}

### Returned allocations
GET {{host}}/api/returns

### 5. Verify asset status is Available again
GET {{host}}/api/assets/1
